1.2 "Derivative Work" means any work that is based on, derived from,
or incorporates the Software or any portion thereof, including but not
limited to: (a) modifications to the original code, (b) code that
implements the same or substantially similar algorithms, patterns,
logic, or functionality, (c) code that calls, interfaces with, or
integrates with the Software, (d) data structures or schemas modeled
on those in the Software, (e) any work that a reasonable person would
consider to be influenced by or based upon the Software, and (f) any
output, result, or data generated by the Software.

1.3 "Trade Secrets" means all proprietary information contained in
the Software including but not limited to: algorithms, formulas,
processes, designs, patterns, know-how, techniques, methods,
improvements, and any other technical or business information that
derives independent economic value from not being generally known.

1.4 "Authorized Use" means use expressly authorized in writing by
the Copyright Holder under a separate executed agreement bearing the
Copyright Holder's signature or digital authentication.

1.5 "Confidential Information" means the Software and all Trade
Secrets, whether or not marked as confidential.

1.6 "Competing Product" means any product, service, application,
platform, or tool that provides, facilitates, or enables money
transmission, cross-border remittance, blockchain-based escrow,
