11. LIQUIDATED DAMAGES

11.1 In lieu of proving actual damages for unauthorized use of the
Software, Licensee agrees to pay liquidated damages as follows:
(a) for unauthorized access or study: five thousand US dollars
(USD 5,000) per instance; (b) for unauthorized use in a Competing
Product: twenty-five thousand US dollars (USD 25,000) per instance;
(c) for unauthorized disclosure: fifteen thousand US dollars
(USD 15,000) per disclosure.

11.2 Each instance of unauthorized use constitutes a separate
violation. Continuing violations accrue daily.

11.3 These liquidated damages represent a genuine pre-estimate of
harm and not a penalty. The parties agree that actual damages would
be difficult or impossible to calculate and that these amounts are
reasonable in light of the anticipated or actual harm.

11.4 If any court determines that the liquidated damages in this
section constitute an unenforceable penalty, the parties agree that
the court may reduce the amount to the maximum enforceable amount,
and the remaining provisions of this License shall continue in full
force.

11.5 The Copyright Holder retains the right to pursue actual damages
in lieu of liquidated damages if actual damages are reasonably
calculable and exceed the liquidated damage amounts.

