33. LICENSE KEY SYSTEM

33.1 The Software includes an integrity verification mechanism that
validates a License Key at startup. The Software shall not execute
without a valid License Key issued by the Copyright Holder.

33.2 License Keys are digitally signed using the Ed25519 algorithm.
The public verification key is embedded in the Software's source code.
The private signing key is held exclusively by the Copyright Holder
and is never distributed.

33.3 A valid License Key is required for: (a) the Software to start,
(b) any Deployment to function, and (c) any test or evaluation
environment to execute the Software's code.

33.4 Licensee shall not: (a) disable, bypass, modify, or tamper with
the License Key validation, (b) share, redistribute, or publish any
License Key, (c) use a License Key issued for one Deployment in a
different Deployment without authorization, or (d) attempt to derive
the private signing key from the public verification key or from any
issued License Key.

33.5 License Keys may include metadata such as permitted Deployment
scope, expiration dates, permitted jurisdictions, and permitted
features. The Software shall enforce these restrictions.

33.6 If the Software detects a missing, invalid, expired, or tampered
License Key, the Software shall refuse to start and shall log the
validation failure for diagnostic purposes. This refusal is an
intentional protection mechanism, not a software defect.

34. ANTI-TAMPER AND INTEGRITY VERIFICATION

34.1 The Software may include integrity verification mechanisms that
detect unauthorized modification of source code, configuration files,
smart contract bytecode, or other critical components.

34.2 Licensee shall not disable, circumvent, or interfere with any
integrity verification mechanism. Any attempt to do so constitutes a
material breach of this License.

34.3 If the Software detects tampering with its integrity, the
Software may: (a) refuse to start, (b) limit functionality, (c) log
the tampering event, or (d) report the tampering to the Copyright
Holder through available channels.

34.4 The presence or absence of integrity verification mechanisms
does not affect the Copyright Holder's rights under this License. The
Copyright Holder retains all remedies regardless of whether integrity
verification is implemented or detects tampering.

